# DTF tier manifest: conda-virtual-shadow-and-cache
#   (artifact-keeper#4555 security + channel facets, #4506; all fixed in 1.11.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + upstreams=mock-conda (the conda-channel-types
# tier's stdlib-python static conda channel on 172.16.<slot>.70; it publishes
# dtfup-alpha 1.0 and 2.0 and dtfup-blocked 1.0 in noarch, and logs every
# request line to stdout).
#
# THE BUGS
# #4555 shadowing  A virtual conda channel merged remote members first and kept
#        the first writer per filename, so an upstream that publishes a name an
#        internal (hosted) member owns sat next to the internal records and won
#        the solve: dependency confusion. Fixed: once a local/staging member has
#        published a name, remote members contribute no records under it,
#        channeldata.json drops their entry, and a download of such a file
#        through the virtual is not proxied upstream.
# #4555 Cache-Control  conda channel documents were `public, max-age=60` even
#        for a request carrying credentials, so a shared cache could store a
#        private channel's (or one caller's merged virtual) index and serve it
#        to the next requester. Fixed: authenticated -> `private`; anonymous
#        responses keep `public`.
# #4555 indexed_timestamp (CEP-47)  hosted records carry a server-set
#        `indexed_timestamp` (ms, the artifact row's created_at), identical
#        across rebuilds and in a virtual's merge.
# #4555 rattler token layout  `/t/<TOKEN>/conda/<repo>/...` (pixi
#        --conda-token) 404'd; only `/conda/t/<TOKEN>/<repo>/...` was mounted.
# #4506  origin policies (denied_upstreams, ...) were evaluated only against an
#        `artifacts` row's origin; a Remote serves proxy-cache content with no
#        such row, so an upstream deny policy never stopped a Remote download.
#        Fixed: Remote content has origin {kind: proxy, upstream_url: <remote's
#        upstream>} and is refused 403 "blocked by the repository's scan
#        policy", cached entries included, and a virtual does not serve it.
#
# RED image: ak-backend:1.10.0 (every fix case). GREEN: 1.11.0 and later.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: one admin login then ~30 authenticated calls back
# to back. UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the remotes' upstream is the mock
# on a private address (the profile also scopes AK_SSRF_ALLOW_PRIVATE_CIDRS).
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-conda"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
